Operations - NRM (54 items) 54 President Direct (1 items) 1 Professional & Cont Studies (1 items) 1 Provost Direct - HC (4 items) 4 Provost Direct - NRM (8 items) 8 Research Administration (11 items) 11 Student Affairs (13 items) 13 University Libraries (2 items) 2 Salary Grade Search 21 filter options found Salary Grade 99C (6 items) 6 A04 (1 items) 1 C03 (5 items) 5 C04 (12 items) 12 C05 (9 items) 9 C06 (4 items) 4 C07 (5 items) 5 C08 (7 items) 7 C09 (1 items) 1 C11 (1 items) 1 S03 (9 items) 9 S04 (11 items) 11 S05 (16 items) 16 S06 (35 items) 35 S07 (40 items) 40 S08 (53 items) 53 S09 (33 items) 33 S10 (25 items) 25 S11 (12 items) 12 S12 (3 items) 3 S13 (3 items) 3 Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs Sort by: Last Updated Last Updated: Newest to Oldest Last Updated: Oldest to Newest Title: A-Z Title: Z-A Lead Custodian Night Shift 493989 Oklahoma City, Oklahoma Campus Operations/Safety Operations - HC S06 The Lead Custodian/Housekeeper independently delivers comprehensive custodial and housekeeping services for campus facilities while training, supervising, and supporting a team of custodians or housekeepers. This position is responsible for ensuring consistent cleanliness standards through the safe and effective use of a variety of chemicals, cleaning appliances, tools, and equipment. Duties require demonstrated competence, appropriate prior training, and strict adherence to established safety and operational procedures. The role also requires the ability to accurately read, understand, and follow written instructions and materials, as well as apply basic math and computer skills in the performance of job responsibilities. Apply now Custodian /Housekeeper 493990 Oklahoma City, Oklahoma Campus Operations/Safety Operations - HC S04 Step into a role that keeps our campus clean, safe, and ready for each day. This position supports the upkeep of offices, residence halls, and public spaces through routine cleaning, sanitation, and organization. From maintaining floors and restrooms to ensuring areas are stocked, orderly, and accessible, this role plays an essential part in creating a comfortable and welcoming environment for everyone. Apply now Research Project Manager 493980 Tulsa, Oklahoma Technology/Research College of Education S10 The Oklahoma Center for Education Policy (OCEP), housed at the University of Oklahoma, seeks a master's-or doctorate-level quantitative education researcher to support and help lead the Center's research agenda on K-12 education policy in Oklahoma. This position will work closely with the Executive Director on applied research projects designed to inform policymakers, education leaders, practitioners, and the public. A central focus of the position will be studying the implementation and impact of state and district policies in Oklahoma, including state efforts to strengthen early reading instruction and improve student outcomes. The researcher will contribute to the design and execution of quantitative studies, support data collection and analysis, help coordinate research activities across the Center, and engage with external stakeholders involved in education policy and practice. This position is well suited for an early-career or mid-career researcher, including recent Ph.D. graduates, advanced doctoral candidates, postdoctoral researchers, or master's-level researchers with strong quantitative skills and an interest in producing timely, policy-relevant research. Apply now Accounting Specialist 493985 Oklahoma City, Oklahoma Administrative Support Operations - HC S06 Join a detail-oriented team where your financial and analytical expertise helps support effective departmental operations. This position performs a variety of accounting, budgeting, and administrative functions, contributing to accurate financial reporting, account management, forecasting, and budget planning.\nThe successful candidate will analyze financial information, prepare reports and forecasts, maintain accounting records, and help monitor departmental accounts for accuracy and compliance. This role also supports annual budget preparation, investigates financial questions, and maintains important departmental data and records.\nThe ideal candidate is organized, analytical, and dependable, with strong attention to detail and the ability to manage complex financial information. This is an excellent opportunity for a professional who enjoys working with numbers, solving problems, and helping a department make informed financial decisions. Apply now Senior Custodian - Floor Crew 493988 Oklahoma City, Oklahoma Campus Operations/Safety Operations - HC S05 Be part of a team that keeps our campus running smoothly. This position will function primarily with the floor crew and plays a key role in maintaining clean, sanitary, and organized environments across offices, residence halls, and shared spaces through consistent, detail-oriented custodial support. Apply now Lead Admin Support Specialist 493987 Oklahoma City, Oklahoma Administrative Support College of Medicine S07 Internal Medicine, division of Endocrinology is looking for a highly motivated Lead Administrative Support Specialist. This individual will maintain office files, schedule various appointments for office personnel, answer incoming phone calls and direct them to the appropriate person, responsible for typing and proof-reading letters, and performs related duties as assigned to successfully Apply now Clinical Research Nurse 493986 Oklahoma City, Oklahoma Technology/Research Provost Direct - HC C07 Established in 2013, the Oklahoma Clinical and Translational Science Institute (OCTSI) serves as a catalyst for clinical and translational research that improves health and healthcare for Oklahomans. As a member of the OCTSI Clinical Research Unit, the Clinical Research Nurse will be responsible for managing recruitment of participants in multiple clinical trials, participating in data collection and entry, as well as ensuring compliance with federal, state and institutional guidelines.\n\nWhy This Role Matters: This is your opportunity to be a part of a high-performing team of clinical research specialists who support groundbreaking trials that bring life-saving medications, healthy interventions and medical devices to the general public. Apply now Athletic Trainer, Football 493983 Norman, Oklahoma Athletics Athletic Department S09 The Athletic Trainer - Football, under the medical-legal supervision of the head team physician and the head athletic trainer, and head football athletic trainer with direct primary responsibility to Football, is responsible for the prevention, evaluation, management and rehabilitation of injury and illness within the University's comprehensive athletic medicine program; empowered with the unchallengeable authority to determine management and return to play of any ill or injured athlete, as the athletic trainer deems appropriate; empowered with unchallengeable authority to cancel or modify any workout for health and safety reasons, as he or she deems appropriate. Apply now Supervisor 493981 Norman, Oklahoma Finance, Grants & Business Operations Continuing Education S08 Join the Center for Public Management (OU CPM) at the University of Oklahoma and be part of a team dedicated to making a daily impact in the lives of Oklahomans. The Administrative Supervisor supports TANF Support Specialists and overall contract deliverables.  The Supervisor provides direct supervision and collaborates with management in the development, implementation and oversight of operational and personnel functions. Apply now Food Services Worker 493982 Norman, Oklahoma Food Services Operations - NRM S03 Cross Village Restaurants, OU's newest dining operation, features unique restaurant concepts. Staff prepare food for a wide variety of concepts including stir fry, barbecue, bold vegan and vegetarian dishes, home cooking, and much more. This position will prepare food following recipes and applying individual portion control standards. Apply now Sr Student Services Specialist 493979 Norman, Oklahoma Student Services Continuing Education S07 The Sr Student Services Specialist is responsible for career exploration activities, job development, building employer relationships and assisting youth with disabilities ages 16-21 to gain and maintain employment. Apply now Food Services Supervisor - Couch Restaurants 493973 Norman, Oklahoma Food Services Operations - NRM S06 The Food Services Supervisor - Couch Restaurants position is responsible for supervising, training and evaluating assigned personnel.  They will determine work priorities, plan schedules, assign and review work. They will serve as an active member of the service team, to include following recipes to prepare food, operating the cash register, and interacting with guests. Apply now Project Coordinator 493971 Norman, Oklahoma Finance, Grants & Business Operations College of Arts & Sciences S08 Join the Carl Albert Center at the University of Oklahoma as the Project Coordinator for a two-year project funded by the National Endowment for the Humanities. The project, Constitutional Foundations Archive, will digitize and make available over 30,000 previously inaccessible documents, photographs, personal papers, and audio files that illustrate the establishment and expansion of federal institutions, state constitutional development, and the evolution of congressional representation in America. Apply now Marketing/Communication Specialist 493965 Oklahoma City, Oklahoma Administrative Support College of Medicine S08 The Department of Pediatrics, Division of Developmental Pediatrics, is seeking a creative, strategic, and highly organized Marketing and Communications Specialist to support and advance the division's mission of improving the health and well-being of children with developmental, behavioral, and learning differences. This role is responsible for developing and implementing comprehensive marketing and communications initiatives that enhance awareness of the division's clinical services, research programs, educational activities, and community outreach efforts. The ideal candidate will possess strong written and verbal communication skills, a talent for storytelling, and experience creating engaging content across multiple platforms. Working collaboratively with faculty, staff, institutional partners, donors, and community stakeholders, the Marketing and Communications Specialist will help promote the division's achievements, strengthen stakeholder engagement, and support fundraising and development initiatives through compelling, mission-driven communications. This position offers an opportunity to make a meaningful impact by helping connect families, healthcare professionals, donors, and community partners with the vital work being accomplished in Developmental Pediatrics. Apply now Contract/Grant Coordinator 493966 Oklahoma City, Oklahoma Administrative Support College of Medicine S08 The Sooner SUCCESS Program is seeking a motivated and detail-oriented Contract/Grant Coordinator to support community-based initiatives that improve outcomes for children, youth, and families across Garfield and Kay Counties. This position plays a vital role in coordinating contracts, grants, and program activities that strengthen partnerships among local agencies, schools, healthcare providers, and community organizations. The ideal candidate will possess strong organizational, communication, and project management skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities while ensuring compliance with contractual and grant requirements. This position offers the opportunity to make a meaningful impact by supporting collaborative efforts that connect families to resources and services, promote community engagement, and advance the mission of Sooner SUCCESS throughout the region. Join a dedicated team committed to building stronger communities and improving the lives of Oklahoma families through coordination, collaboration, and service excellence. Apply now PEAK - Receptionist - CECPD 493978 Norman, Oklahoma Oklahoma City, Oklahoma Administrative Support PEAK - Temporary Human Resources Do you like to interact with the public and help them resolve their questions? If so, join us at the Center for Early Childhood Professional Development (CECPD) as our temporary receptionist. CECPD is a department within the College of Continuing Education at the University of Oklahoma. We provide many programs for the Child Care field throughout the State of Oklahoma. Apply now PEAK - Finance and Operations Assistant 493977 Norman, Oklahoma PEAK - Temporary Human Resources The Finance and Operations Assistant would provide administrative support to the PACS Sr. Finance Analyst, Lead Operations Coordinator and Data Analyst. Job duties would include financial invoicing, creating financial and data analysis reports for PACS unit directors, reconciling bi-weekly payroll reports, assisting with faculty and staff hiring and onboarding, and other various duties related to the daily operation of the college. Apply now PEAK - Lead Admin Support Spec - Dept. of  Medicine - Endocrinology 493976 Norman, Oklahoma Oklahoma City, Oklahoma Administrative Support PEAK - Temporary Human Resources Performs support-oriented job duties to a Department Head or Manager.  Duties are complex and of an advanced nature, to include but not limited to maintaining files, scheduling appointments, managing inventory, typing, preparing reports and correspondence, distributing information, conducting research and computation, managing office procedures, assisting with budget preparation, and coordinating activities.  Serves as a payroll coordinator and resource to other support personnel.  May supervise support staff. Apply now PEAK - Senior Administrative Support Specialist - College of Dentistry 493975 Norman, Oklahoma Oklahoma City, Oklahoma Administrative Support PEAK - Temporary Human Resources The Senior Administrative Support Specialist provides advanced administrative, operational, and customer service support for the Comprehensive Care, Endodontics, and Operative Dentistry divisions within the OU College of Dentistry. This position serves as a key resource for faculty, staff, residents, and students by coordinating daily operations, managing departmental processes, supporting academic and clinical activities, and ensuring efficient communication across multiple areas. Apply now MARKETING/PR SPECIALIST 493968 Norman, Oklahoma Arts, Media & Communications Provost Direct - NRM S08 The Sam Noble Oklahoma Museum of Natural History is seeking a Marketing/PR Specialist who will be responsible for effectively promoting and marketing the museum and its mission. Responsible for identifying audiences, locally, regionally and nationally, and developing, implementing, and managing a strategic integrated communication plant to reach those audiences. Will represent the museum in a professional manner. Apply now Academic Advisor 493969 Norman, Oklahoma Student Services College of Business S07 The Michael F. Price College of Business is seeking a supportive and service-oriented professional to join our team as an Academic Advisor. This position provides individualized guidance to undergraduate business students as they navigate academic requirements, explore educational opportunities, and make progress toward graduation. Apply now Senior Financial Aid Specialist MoneyCoach 493964 Norman, Oklahoma Student Services Enrollment Management S07 The MoneyCoach connects individually with incoming and current students to provide financial coaching services which may include financial literacy, budgeting, and counseling on financial aid options to fund their education through graduation. We seek individuals who exhibit integrity, care, intentionality, and innovation. Apply now Custodian - Athletics 493962 Norman, Oklahoma Campus Operations/Safety Operations - NRM S04 Facilities Management is hiring Custodial team members to work in our Custodial Services division. Custodial Services performs routine and specialized services, ensuring a healthy and clean environment to promote the University's mission. Apply now Academic Advisor 493961 Norman, Oklahoma Student Services College of Engineering S07 The Gallogly College of Engineering's Williams Student Services Center (WSSC) is seeking an Academic Advisor to support our undergraduate programs. The WSSC academic advising staff is responsible for supporting academic success and personal development of students in the college, as well as responding to inquiries, monitoring student progress, maintaining student records, and assisting students with navigating university requirements and college policies/procedures. Apply now Work Control Specialist 493955 Norman, Oklahoma Administrative Support Operations - NRM S06 The University of Oklahoma is seeking a customer-focused and detail-oriented Work Control Specialist to support Facilities Management operations and serve as a primary point of contact for campus service requests. Apply now Food Services Worker - Cross Restaurants 493945 Norman, Oklahoma Food Services Operations - NRM S03 Cross Restaurants, features two unique food court concepts. Staff prepare food for a wide variety of concepts: barbecue, bold vegan and vegetarian dishes, home cooking, and much more. Apply now Radiological Technologist 493772 Norman, Oklahoma Health/Wellness Services Student Affairs C06 Goddard Health Center is the ambulatory care facility on the Norman campus, providing primary care services to students, faculty, staff, and their dependents. If you're looking for a meaningful career in a supportive academic setting, consider joining our team. At Goddard Health Center, you'll have the opportunity to make a real impact on the health and well-being of the University of Oklahoma community. Apply now PEAK - Food Service - Cross Restaurants 493957 Norman, Oklahoma Food Services PEAK - Temporary Human Resources Cross Restaurants is now hiring enthusiastic food services staff through PEAK!  In this fast-paced and team-oriented role, you’ll help prepare and serve delicious meals while delivering excellent customer service. Responsibilities include following recipes and portion standards, safely combining ingredients, prepping ingredients for production lines, operating a variety of kitchen equipment, and serving food with courtesy and care. You’ll be expected to maintain a clean and sanitary workspaces and wash dishes. . Sandwiches, smash burgers, tacos, smoothies, and more are all made to order at Cross.  Day shifts and late closing shift available 7 days a week.  Part-time and temporary full-time schedules available! Apply now Program Manager 493953 Oklahoma City, Oklahoma Administrative Support College of Public Health S10 Responsible for program management and oversight of day-to-day operations and provides support to the department chair for the Department of Biostatistics & Epidemiology. Performs various duties as needed to successfully fulfill the function of the position. Apply now PEAK - Research Technician - Luong Lab 493952 Oklahoma City, Oklahoma PEAK - Temporary Technology/Research Human Resources The Luong Lab at the OU Health Campus is filling this position through PEAK Temporary Staffing.\n\nProvides assistance to a research staff by conducting simple research experiments, collecting data and samples, keeping records, conducting literature searches, analyzing data, and preparing reports Apply now Displaying 1 - 30 of 361 in total ‹ 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 9 … 12 13 › Powered by PageUp Contact Human Resources We serve the Norman, Oklahoma City, and Tulsa Campuses Accessibility Sustainability HIPAA OU Jobs Search Policies Legal Notices Copyright Resources And Offices OU Report It! Updated 9/11/2025 by Human Resources : HrTalent@ou.edu Candidate Details We use cookies to give you a customiz