an excellent opportunity for someone who enjoys both leadership and hands-on recruiting and wants to make a lasting impact on the organization. Apply now Student Union Assistant Director 493266 Norman, Oklahoma Administrative Support Featured Technical Operations - NRM S09 The Oklahoma Memorial Union (OMU) at the University of Oklahoma serves as a vibrant hub for campus life, bringing together students, faculty, staff, and visitors through dynamic programs, events, and services. We are seeking a highly organized and strategic leader to join our team as the Assistant Director of the Oklahoma Memorial Union. This role provides a unique opportunity to shape the University's centralized scheduling system, oversee large-scale event operations, and lead innovative initiatives that enhance the campus experience across multiple locations. Reporting to the Director of the OMU, the Assistant Director plays a critical leadership role in managing scheduling systems, advancing operational efficiencies, and supervising both professional and student staff. The ideal candidate is a collaborative problem-solver with strong technical and operational expertise, and a high level of technical proficiency in utilizing and adapting to technology systems that support centralized scheduling, event operations, and process improvement, capable of balancing complex logistics while driving continuous improvement. This position is well-suited for a professional who thrives in a fast-paced, service-oriented environment and is passionate about supporting student engagement and institutional success. Apply now Senior Accounting Specialist 493747 Oklahoma City, Oklahoma Featured Student Services Clerical Administration & Finance - HC S07 Looking for a stable career where your financial and customer service skills make a difference? Join the OU Health Campus Bursar's Office as a Senior Accounting Specialist. In this role, you'll develop specialized expertise in student accounts and loan servicing while assisting students and graduates, processing financial transactions, maintaining accurate records, and ensuring compliance with federal and institutional regulations. Apply now PEAK - Talent Acquisition Specialist 492896 Norman, Oklahoma Featured PEAK - Temporary Admin Staff hourly Clerical Professional hourly Human Resources Join Our Team as a Recruiting & Applicant Support Specialist!\n\nIf you love helping people, staying organized, and keeping a fast‑moving workflow on track, this role is a great fit. We’re looking for a detail‑oriented, customer‑focused professional to support applicants, hiring managers, and departmental users throughout the recruiting process. Apply now Food Services Supervisor - Panera 493129 Norman, Oklahoma Featured Food Services Service/Maintenance Operations - NRM S06 Panera at the Oklahoma Memorial Union is seeking a dependable and detail-oriented PM Supervisor to serve as a first-line leader overseeing evening food service operations. This role is responsible for coordinating food preparation, production, and service while ensuring quality, efficiency, and compliance with university and health department standards. The PM Supervisor plays a key role in maintaining smooth daily operations by monitoring food quality, managing supplies, supporting financial processes, and providing excellent customer service. This position requires strong organizational skills, attention to detail, and the ability to lead a team in a fast-paced dining environment. · Coordinates food preparation and serving of food. Monitors food preparation methods, portion sizes, and presentation of the food. · Oversees inventory and procurement. Ensures adequate supplies, materials and equipment are available. · Monitors the safety and cleanliness of the facility and equipment. Adheres to university and Health Department quality standards. · Assists with preparation of master menus. · Oversees operation of cash register, prepares daily cash report. · Responds to customer inquiries regarding food quality, service, or accommodations and resolves the problems and routine complaints. · Prepares various reports for management regarding the operation of the facility, sanitation, food preparation and any complaints or problems. · Maintains regulatory, compliance, and operational records. · Opens and secures facility. · May assume responsibility for a second shift. · Attends meetings, in-service training, and work related classes. · Performs various duties as needed to successfully fulfill the functions of the position. Apply now Displaying all 5 entries Powered by PageUp Contact Human Resources We serve the Norman, Oklahoma City, and Tulsa Campuses Accessibility Sustainability HIPAA OU Jobs Search Policies Legal Notices Copyright Resources And Offices OU Report It! Updated 9/11/2025 by Human Resources : HrTalent@ou.edu Candidate Details We use cookies to give you a customized experience such as job recommendations and to analyze our traffic.  Through the use of cookies, the University will know what’s working and what’s not.  That information is then used to keep our content fresh and relevant to You the user. You consent to our cookies if you click “I Accept.”  By clicking “I Accept” you agree to the use of the Privacy Policy , which includes the use of cookies.  If you click on “I Do Not Accept,” then we will not use cookies, but you may have a deteriorated user experience.  You can change your settings by click on the Settings link on the top right of the device. Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. Performance Cookies These cookies 